{
  "slug": "idle-timing",
  "name": "Idle Timing",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "- Injects timing block to prompts (not user-visible) covering local date-time, idle time (since agent turn ended), and prior turn execution time.\n- Shows `[after Xm Ys]` to user via post submit hook to indicate how long it was between that prompt and agent finishing prior turn.\n- Provides statusline integration for idle time.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `idle-time-reset` (Clear the idle-timing state and log for the current session, or all sessions), `idle-time-setup` (Show paste-ready snippet to wire the idle-timing fragment into your existing statusline), `idle-time-status` (Run a one-shot self-test of the idle-timing plugin (data dir, hook scripts, logs))\n- **Hooks** (3): `UserPromptSubmit`, `Stop`, `PreCompact`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install idle-timing@claude-community` from `clankercode/claude-inject-idle-time`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 3,
    "command": 3
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
